      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "sod-on-birch-bark",
          "status": "canonical",
          "note": "Turf (torvtak) over a birch-bark waterproofing layer, retained at the edge by a log or board; matches the family's pitch_snow_dominant band (18-30 deg family / 22-30 deg this node's own c04)."
        },
        {
          "id": "split-shingle",
          "status": "canonical",
          "note": "Riven shingle on the steeper, rain-dominant roofs; matches the family's pitch_rain_or_shingle band (35-45 deg)."
        }
      ],
      "rule": "Roof material tracks the same two-band split the family's own roof_pitch binding already establishes: sod over birch bark where snow dominates (22-30 degrees, c04), split shingle where rain does (35-45 degrees).",
      "sources": [
        "scandinavian-log-vernacular.c04",
        "scandinavian-log-vernacular.json defining_characteristics"
      ],
      "note": " UNJUDGED, stated 24 Aug 2026 (OQ 19): this slot names `roof_pitch` as its determiner and `roof_pitch` is empty on this kit, so the choice between the two variants here is not actually decided by anything. It is not a free choice either -- sod on birch bark needs a shallow pitch to stay on and a split shingle needs a steep one to shed -- which is exactly why the determination was declared. Until `roof_pitch` is bound this reads as specified and is not."
    },
